        "id": 7892,
        "name": "Pydro",
        "username": "Pydro",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/pydro/{size}/1844_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-05-05T16:44:25.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>We now know that it is IL on Prophetic Vision. What I don't understand is how is this \"prophetic\" or a \"vision.\" If Visionary knows what will happen because she lived it, this wouldn't be called a \"prophecy\" or a \"vision.\" The only thing I can think of is that she would might see Legacy doing something less than heroic (e.g. punching someone a little too hard) and get a flash of what he can become. If this is true, then the death of YL is not a \"greatly traumatic event that completely overturns Legacy's current moral code\" but rather the \"straw that broke the camel's back.\" This could have great implications as to the nature of Legacy and his inner battles.</p><p>Of course there are probably better explanations, so bring them on!</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:38:16.968Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
